    "turn_text": "well if you know the record moment uh... it was all the hours up until i can remember stranger time then you know uh... we would all week at a very tense week we'd work through many conversations uh... and felt like we'd finally reached the finish line and and and then uh... you know we were expecting mac gates in larm bober to vote for kevin macarthi and they both would present which left us a vote short and so at that moment i think there's just a lot of emotion a lot of uh... you know like i say it was a very tense time and you know the role i tried to play all week was to reduce tension uh... try to be a peacemaker try to be uh... someone who the listener And so at that moment, I realized what we needed was to make sure that we kept people calm and that we kept talking. And so when I saw Representative Rogers, I could tell by his body language that he was upset. And so I just, you know, did what I could do to try to keep that from escalating into something else. The real shame of it is, you know, I sort of reached the gravity by the shoulders. And as I was pulling him back, he was kind of fighting against me and my hand flipped. And it went up to his face. It looked like I was trying to muzzle him. So it looked a lot more dramatic than it really was. I just kind of pulled him back and kind of got him out of that situation. But anyway, you know, of all my goals in life, I've never had a goal of trending. But apparently that's happened.",
