    "turn_idx": 76,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, I'm not, I'm not happy about it. You know, it was one of the saddest moments of my life, really, just to see the breakdown on the house floor, to see tensions like that. To me, I was sad about it and, you know, I certainly didn't want people looking at me. You know, I'm not the kind of person that's out there saying, look at me, look at me. You know, I'm a servant of the people and try to get things done. And, you know, most of the work I do in Congress is behind the scenes. Just deliver results from the folks I represent. So, you know, I really wasn't comfortable. You know, I've gotten so many messages, hundreds and hundreds of text messages from all over the world, frankly. And I don't feel comfortable being called a hero or being thanked for what I did because, you know, it was a sad time and I'm just glad we got through it.",
